  "diagnosis": "The synthesizer's hypothesis is correct in shape but wrong in mechanism. Using $('body *').each() walks the DOM in document order, which IS visual order, so ordering isn't the bug. The real bug is the regex anchor `^Auction Starts`: cheerio's .text() on an ancestor element concatenates ALL descendant text, so when .each() iterates the outer container, `text` starts with body-level content (e.g. 'Running Auctions Auction Starts...'), failing `^`. When iteration reaches the leaf element that uniquely contains 'Auction Starts mm/dd/yyyy hh:mm AM ET', it MAY match — but only if the time string is in the SAME leaf node as the label. RealAuction's typical markup splits the label into a <span class='AuctionType_lbl'> and the time into a sibling element, so no leaf .text() ever starts with 'Auction Starts' followed by the date. Additionally the `text.length < 100` cap further restricts the match. Result: currentStartTime stays undefined for every row, hence auctionDate=NULL on 199/199. The section-header detection has the same fragility but happens to work because 'Running Auctions'/'Auctions Waiting' are usually in their own header element. No saved HTML probe exists (no probe-artifacts/realauction*.html), so the exact DOM cannot be confirmed without re-running inspect-realauction-calendar.ts.",
