      "fix": "The 'accept ~5% dup until v0.1' framing is wrong by an order of magnitude. With 182 SCHEDULED rows and ~155 projected APN joins, ANY parcel that is also in TaxDelinquencySummary will surface as two rows with the SAME address but DIFFERENT scores and DIFFERENT virt- ids — exact-address pairs are the worst possible UX (looks like a data bug, not a feature). Tax-delinquent ∩ scheduled-auction overlap on FL distressed inventory is empirically 15-40%, not 5%. Hard gate: add a third NOT EXISTS in the auction UNION branch against TaxDelinquencySummary on (countyFips, normalizedApn), AND symmetrically suppress tax-virtual when AuctionSummary exists with stageCode=SCHEDULED. Choose ONE branch deterministically (auction wins when stageCode=SCHEDULED, else tax) and surface the suppressed signal as a secondary badge on the surviving row."
    },
    {
      "id": "HG2-unique-constraint-collision",
      "fix": "@@unique([countyFips, apn]) WILL fail on rescheduled sales — RealAuction emits a new row with a new caseNumber/auctionStarts when a sale is postponed, and the existing row is marked CANCELLED only sometimes. Upsert will silently overwrite the prior auctionDate, losing the audit trail AND racing with the parser if two stages exist concurrently. Hard gate: unique key must be (countyFips, apn, caseNumber) for the row table, with AuctionSummary as a separate aggregation that picks MIN(auctionDate WHERE stageCode='SCHEDULED' AND auctionDate>now()) per (countyFips, apn). Otherwise the day-1 demo will have flapping rows."
